      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-06T03:45:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Here I am, to defend my characterization of Voss knocking six shards off OblivAeon as relatively easy!</p>\n<p>It took the combined might of Ra and the Ennead to do enough damage to create ONE OblivAeon shard. Ra! And Atum, who vaporized a city! AND all the rest of them! Apparently, Voss is at least six times as powerful as that.</p>\n<p>It's not because Voss is in the base set that I am skeptical of his power. It's that I never lose against him! Dawn is much harder. Heck, <em>The</em> <em>Ennead</em> is harder. This power level out of Voss is just so...surprising. Compared to the strike that the Egyptian pantheon delivered to OblivAeon, it sure does seem easy for Voss to knock chips off the guy.</p>",
