    {
      "id": 223794,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-06T23:26:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>In a sense, he created both.&nbsp; Yes, the one with the time rewind he initiated is the Sentinel Comics universe.&nbsp; But because he caused a fork, OblivAeon was in only one of the two.&nbsp; Without Setback, the canon universe would have been one in which Rook City was destroyed but OblivAeon was defeated.&nbsp; Because the heroes succeeded in that timeline, super-powered individuals wouldn't be on the outs with the general population, and because Voss would have been there, the Mist Storm wouldn't have been possible.&nbsp; So it would have been somewhat darker than the Comics Universe timeline, but much less dark than the Mist Storm one.</p>\n<p>But yes, the simple answer is that his action led to what happened in the RPG timeline, and the one in which he didn't act was the Mist Storm timeline.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:01.750Z",
